        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition>
                "An Atom is one persistent GIL-specific semantic identity, including Gods, Titans or glyph-bearing referents. A glyph such as † is a versioned notation/behavioral role of the underlying Atom, never an additional Atom identity by itself. Atom meaning, notation, provenance, qualification, operational state and source correspondence have independent versions and context-dependent selection."@en;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote>
                "The Atom IRI stays stable when § is superseded by † as Tyr notation. Glyph triggers such as ø and ∂ remain Atoms whose authorized operation is not G0002 qualification. A new version or stronger status does not mint another Atom."@en;
